  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Navigation Restriction**\n\nI\'ve got it - the application *must* be contained within a single view. That clarifies things! It means focusing entirely on tabs, sheets, or sub-views, no separate navigation. Now I can build the core architecture without worrying about complex navigation systems, which is great.\n\n\n**Defining Widget Scope**\n\nI\'ve realized this is perfect for the single-view concept. The Android widget sync request means we can configure the URL, port, key, and path within the single view. It will include a header, a configuration card, action buttons, a task preview, and a log footer, to stay organized.\n\n\n**Designing Widget Components**\n\nI\'m solidifying the widget\'s architecture now. The `AndroidManifest.xml` and `AppWidgetProvider` class are planned, along with RemoteViews for the layout. I\'m leaning toward a clean design: header with the name and refresh, a list of current tasks (3-5), and PendingIntents for task interactions, to handle completion toggling directly. It makes it all so convenient to trigger a BroadcastReceiver or service to call the PC API.\n\n\n**Structuring Data Storage**\n\nI\'m now focusing on data storage for the widget. I\'ve considered storing everything in a Room database or splitting it between `SharedPreferences` for configuration and Room for tasks. Ultimately, storing both configuration and tasks in Room is the most flexible approach, or storing tasks in Room and configuration in `SharedPreferences`. I\'ve defined a `Task` entity with fields for ID, text, completion status, note path, and line number within the Obsidian file. The ID will be either a UUID or a hash of the content for Obsidian compatibility.\n\n\n**Analyzing API Endpoint Options**\n\nI\'m now diving into the API design for task completion. The goal is to support multiple server setups, which could be anything from the Obsidian Local REST API plugin to a custom script. For the Markdown mode, I\'ll need to GET the file, modify the line (e.g., `- [ ]` to `- [x]`), and PUT the updated content. I\'m prioritizing flexibility.\n\n\n**Defining API Modes**\n\nI\'ve got two API modes mapped out now: Markdown Mode, which handles raw text GET/PUT, and JSON API Mode for structured data. The settings toggle between these modes will allow users to specify their preferred endpoints, like `/vault/Todo.md` for Markdown or `/tasks` for JSON. The simplicity of Markdown Mode is striking, with only needing GET and PUT requests.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Layer**\n\nI\'m now implementing the data layer. I\'m focusing on a `TaskEntity` for storage, a `TaskDao` for database interaction, and `AppDatabase` as the Room database. The `ObsidianSyncRepository` handles remote fetching, local updates, and synchronization, with Markdown and JSON parsing built-in.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Widget Data Display**\n\nI\'m now figuring out the widget display. I\'ll extend `AppWidgetProvider` with custom remote views for the layout. A refresh button will trigger a short-lived sync task to update the widget. Task list clicks will trigger broadcasts for background toggling, syncing, and database/widget refreshes. I need a scrolling list in `RemoteViews`, which is standard! The `RemoteViewsService` and `RemoteViewsFactory` will populate dynamic items. I\'m choosing a scrolling database list.\n\n\n**Refining Widget Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the widget\'s visuals. I\'m aiming for a professional look with a `ListView`, complete with a clean \"empty state\" message (\"No pending tasks. Cool!\") when there are no items to display. I\'ll include checkboxes next to each task for easy interaction. To ensure robustness, I\'m developing a `RemoteViewsService` and `RemoteViewsFactory` called `ObsidianWidgetService`. I\'ve prepared a `metadata.json` file with name and description details, and updated the `app_name` in `strings.xml`. I\'m changing the `applicationId` in `build.gradle.kts` and making sure there are no remaining instances of the default placeholder.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 253511233
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
