  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting Widget Provider**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of `ObsidianTodoWidgetProvider.kt`. My focus is on ensuring it can effectively manage widget updates. Specifically, I\'m setting up the intent for the `widget_refresh_button` and configuring the RemoteViewsService adapter for the `widget_list_view` when triggered by an update call.\n\n\n**Defining Click Actions**\n\nI\'ve set up the template intent for list item clicks, broadcasting `ACTION_TOGGLE_TASK` with task ID and completion status. I\'ve also implemented the broadcast receiver actions: refreshing the widget now triggers a background sync using Coroutines before updating. For task clicks, I\'m calling `ObsidianSyncRepository` in a coroutine to toggle task completion. Finally, I ensured that `PendingIntent` are properly set up using the provider.\n\n\n**Confirming Implementation Details**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the click interception strategy within the list widget, implementing `setOnClickFillInIntent` for both the status icon and text. This approach seems robust and elegant. Now, I\'m focusing on the supporting infrastructure: confirming the necessity of both the widget provider and the RemoteViewsService, and planning the implementation of the `RemoteViewsFactory` to load data directly from the `AppDatabase`.\n\n\n**Implementing RemoteViewsService**\n\nI\'m now in the thick of implementing `ObsidianWidgetService` and the associated `ObsidianWidgetFactory`. I\'ve established the database connection and the data access object. I have established that the `onDataSetChanged` method is triggered on a background thread as expected. Currently, I\'m verifying data population from the database, focusing on retrieving all tasks directly. The rest of the `RemoteViewsFactory` interface is already implemented.\n\n\n**Refining Item Representation**\n\nI\'m now refining how tasks are visually represented within the widget. I\'ve encountered a limitation with directly manipulating paint flags in `RemoteViews` across various SDK versions, so I\'ve pivoted to setting the status icon based on task completion. I\'m dynamically updating the icon, using a checkmark for completed tasks, and a checkbox for incomplete ones.\n\n\n**Finalizing List Click Logic**\n\nI\'ve just finished the implementation for click logic within each list item of the widget. I\'m dynamically updating the `RemoteViews` with an intent to toggle the task completion. I\'m focusing on handling both the status icon and the text click events. I\'m ensuring the correct intent extras are passed: `task_id` and `is_completed`. Finally, I\'m overriding `getLoadingView`, `getViewTypeCount`, `getItemId`, and `hasStableIds` for robust data handling.\n\n\n"
