  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Widget Core**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the `ObsidianTodoWidgetProvider.kt` file. My focus is on the crucial receivers: `onUpdate()` which will manage layouts, refresh intents, and list collection templates; and `onReceive()`, which is designed to intercept widget button clicks and item toggles.\n\n\n**Handling Refresh Intents**\n\nI\'ve been examining the behavior of `onReceive()` and how it should manage intents. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the `ACTION_REFRESH` intent, which is triggered by the sync button. I\'ve concluded that `goAsync()` is the right method for safe async work inside `BroadcastReceiver`. I will use a coroutine to handle synchronization and widget updates within `onReceive()`.\n\n\n**Managing Task Toggle Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `ACTION_TOGGLE_TASK` functionality into `onReceive()`. I\'ve implemented logic to extract the `taskId` and completion status from the intent. I\'m using `goAsync()` to ensure safe asynchronous operations, launching a coroutine within `Dispatchers.IO` to handle task toggling and widget updates.\n\n\n"
