  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Addressing Build Errors**\n\nI encountered a build timeout/network error, which might be transient, so I\'ll try recompiling. If that fails, I\'ll shift focus to UI creation to avoid further delays. Compilation can be time-consuming, but hopefully the platform will cooperate this time around.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI Design**\n\nI\'ve decided to prioritize the UI design using Jetpack Compose, leaning into an Obsidian-themed aesthetic. The goal is a dark, slate-themed canvas with specific color choices: light gray for primary text, a secondary gray for subtext, and the brand color amethyst for accents. I\'m focusing on the primary dark background, secondary card background, and card outlines, as well as features for a Status Bar/Connection Checker, to confirm synchronicity.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration Card**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the configuration card design, aiming for an expandable or tabbed format. I\'m implementing inputs for IP address, port (defaulting to 8089), sync mode, and note/endpoint path. I\'ve also added options for an optional API token or header key for enhanced security. \"Save Settings\" and \"Sync Now\" buttons are essential for functionality.\n\\n\\n\n**Defining Task List Structure**\n\nI\'m structuring task lists into modern tabbed lists: Focus Blocks and Floating Micro-tasks. The key distinction is time stamps. I\'ll parse markdown tasks; those with time stamps, such as \"18:30 - 19:00\", are \"Focus Blocks\", while those without or under untimed headings are \"Floating Micro-tasks\"!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will inspect `/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/Task.kt` using the `view_file` tool to see how we can expand it to parse and support timed focus blocks and categories."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 710017537
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
