    thinking: "**Considering Code Updates**\n\nOkay, I\'m shifting gears. I was eager to create that markdown and JSON parser, but I need to ensure it integrates seamlessly. Now, I\'m focusing on `ObsidianSyncRepository.kt` to identify areas for improvement or necessary prior readings. Specifically, I\'m digging into `parseAndSaveMarkdown`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Heading Structure**\n\nI\'ve been examining how to structure headings while parsing markdown lines. I think tracking `currentHeading`, `currentCategory`, and `currentSubCategory` is a good way to go. I can parse headings using a regex like `^#+\\s+(.+)$`. I\'m starting to think about how to categorize content based on header text, such as recognizing \"FOCUS BLOCKS,\" \"UNTIMED,\" and potential level-3 subcategories using case-insensitive comparisons.\n\n\n**Refining Task Parsing**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the parsing of checklist items, especially with time ranges. I\'m experimenting with regex to extract checkbox status, task text, and now time ranges if they exist. I think I\'ve landed on a good regex: `^([0-2]?\\d:[0-5]\\d\\s*-\\s*[0-2]?\\d:[0-5]\\d)\\s+(.*)$`. If that matches, I can split the time range from the display title.\n\n\n**Implementing Time Range Logic**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I realized that any task within a time range, under a `## FOCUS BLOCKS` heading, should automatically categorize itself as a \"FOCUS_BLOCK.\" The code I\'m writing reflects this, applying it during markdown parsing and ensuring consistent categorization. I\'m also ensuring this logic is applied uniformly to JSON sync, by applying the same time-range regex to `text` from items in `parseAndSaveJson`. I\'m going to create a helper method for parsing a task text to make this reusable, and define `ParsedTextDetails`.\n\n\n**Defining Text Parsers**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `TextDetails` logic, and adding support for a single time prefix, in addition to time ranges, which should still categorize the tasks. I\'ve defined regex patterns to handle both scenarios, improving the categorization accuracy of the tasks. I\'m prioritizing the single time case as an alternative.\n\n\n"
