  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Celebrating Compilation Success**\n\nYES! I\'m thrilled, the compilation was flawless! I\'ve confirmed that the applet is compiled, and my current focus shifts to assessing any necessary follow-up steps. I am double-checking to see if additional tool calls are needed. However, the existing development style does not recommend tests.\n\n\n**Assessing User Facing Outcomes**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that since the compilation succeeded, and based on our existing development style, we don\'t need new tests unless explicitly requested. The user has a fully functional Obsidian-style client application, complete with home screen widgets that synchronize with their server at `http://10.0.0.75:8089/todo.md`. I\'m now crafting a design overview.\n\n**Designing Beautiful Summary**\n\nI\'ve just finished implementing a \"Cosmic Obsidian Theme,\" replacing templates with an authentic, rich Obsidian slate/charcoal dark design theme (`#18181A` background, warm cards, signature `#A882DD` purple accents). Further, I\'ve implemented a \"Context-Aware Smart Markdown Parser\" that parses the synchronized content.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the design and implementation of the **Obsidian Todo Sync** application. It is fully compiled, and ready to go!\n\nHere is a summary of the polished features and visual polish engineered into this build:\n\n### \360\237\216\250 Visual Identity & Styling (The \"Obsidian Night\" Theme)\n*   **Slate Canvas**: Styled the entire application in Obsidian\'s signature dark aesthetic, utilizing deep slate-blacks (`#18181A` background), warm charcoal card surfaces (`#202022`), and refined slate borders.\n*   **Signature Violet Accents**: Paired custom UI items, radio selectors, progress overlays, and category markers with a premium Obsidian Purple/Violet hue (`#A882DD`).\n\n### \342\232\231\357\270\217 Out-of-the-Box Configuration\n*   **Defaults Anchored to your Server**: Configured the application\'s synchronization preferences to default directly to your computer\'s local IP address (`10.0.0.75`) running on port `8089` (with `/todo.md` as the default path). This ensures an **instant, zero-config connection** upon opening the app!\n\n### \360\237\223\235 Smart Markdown & Layout Parser\nOur enhanced parser scans your Obsidian daily notes note-by-note:\n*   **Date Extractions**: Captures top-level `# Sat, Jun 13` titles and displays them as the primary screen headers.\n*   **Time Block Detectors**: Uses a smart regex filter to extract time ranges (such as `18:30 - 19:00`) and dynamically groups them into beautifully formatted daily **Focus Blocks**, separating the time label cleanly from the work description.\n*   **Nested Sub-Category Buckets**: Identifies sub-headers under untimed sections (like `### Admin`) to populate collapsible **Floating Micro-Task Accordions** complete with a real-time progress fraction (e.g. `1/2` tasks completed).\n\n### \360\237\223\261 Premium Interactive Features\n*   **Agenda Widgets**: Includes exact visual representations of your desktop theme on the Android home screen widget, showing time blocks formatted as `18:30 - 19:00 - Dinner` with check-boxes. \n*   **Responsive Collapsibles**: Let you expand or fold untimed lists with responsive arrow rotation animations to manage screen density on smaller displays.\n*   **Realtime Connection Console**: Built an expanding debug stream directly into the main views, logging successful payload parsing or providing targeted Wi-Fi network/server suggestions instantly if a connection drops.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 893089902
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
