    thinking: "**Locating Missing File**\n\nI\'m currently trying to pinpoint the location of the `todo.md` file. While it seems Obsidian Sync *should* make the Markdown file accessible locally, it appears to be nested within my vault, specifically under `02_Journal/01_Daily/YYYY-MM-DD` within the root folder. I am now exploring whether the widget can directly link to the web app or needs local file access.\n\n\n**Refining File Access**\n\nI\'ve clarified the file path, realizing `todo.md` isn\'t a separate file, but the daily note itself, located at `/02_Journal/01_Daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md`. Given today is 2026-06-13, the target is dynamic! Now considering how to handle this dynamically: can the app automatically calculate the path from metadata or use a template (e.g., `[date]`)? If the path is empty, I\'ll default it to `/02_Journal/01_Daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md` automatically.\n\n\n**Investigating Web App Sync**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the remote server! This user\'s setup involves a to-do web app at `http://10.0.0.75:8089/`, likely an Obsidian-based dashboard or custom application. My current challenge involves determining the best method to interact with the web app. Can I fetch tasks, toggle their status, or simply link to it via the widget? I need to figure out if it supports API interactions or requires direct linking. Let me explore the \"Obsidian Local REST API\" or \"Obsidian Web\" plugins again.\n\n\n**Exploring Web App Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the web app, imagining this dark-themed scheduler at `http://10.0.0.75:8089/` with its focus blocks and floating micro-tasks. I\'m focusing on its API, or lack thereof. Should I make a smart fallback system? If the local Obsidian REST API (typically port 27124) can fetch and parse the daily note, that\'s ideal. If not, can I fetch tasks or markdown directly from the web app? Or should I let the user configure the endpoints?\n\n\n**Implementing Date Substitution**\n\nI\'ve got a breakthrough! I realized that if the path contains `{YYYY-MM-DD}` or `{date}`, or defaults to `/02_Journal/01_Daily/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md`, I can automatically substitute the current date. Today\'s date is `2026-06-13`, so the path becomes `/02_Journal/01_Daily/2026-06-13.md` \342\200\223 elegant and problem-solving!\n\nI\'ve confirmed the widget will dynamically pull task checklist values, toggle completion, and sync back to the local file. Also, the widget will open the web app URL. This addresses the question of direct linking versus feature recreation!\n\n\n"
