  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Summarizing Design Accomplishments**\n\nThe build completed successfully! I\'ve formulated `getResolvedPathOrEndpoint()`, dynamically resolving paths with date tokens like `{YYYY-MM-DD}`. The function intercepts file paths to check for placeholders, and returns an endpoint without a file extension. I will ensure this is presented cleanly and accurately to the user.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully updated the app and widget, addressing both the local file pathway and adding an elegant browser integration. Here is what has been configured:\n\n- **Dynamic Journal File Paths**: To support daily notes organized under your vault layout, the application now supports dynamic run-time calendar resolving. You can use placeholders like `{YYYY-MM-DD}` or `{date}` (e.g. `/02_Journal/01_Daily/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md`). The app will automatically substitute today\'s local date (`2026-06-13.md`) when syncing. The default config path has been updated to use this dynamic folder structure out of the box.\n- **Home Screen Web Redirect**: The home screen widget now functions as a unified direct link. Clicking on the header text or the logo area of the widget automatically launches your default web browser and directs it to your hosted web app at `http://[Your PC IP]:[Port]/` for full details.\n- **Bi-Directional Action Control**: Checked items clicked directly inside your widget list will continue to invoke background REST edits to check or uncheck tasks and synchronize them with your PC database, while larger layout sections direct you back to the full web browser experience.\n- **Configuration Help**: The in-app setup panel has been updated with real-time helper text guiding you on how to format daily notes."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 855414411
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
